## Current State and Evidence

### What Has Been Demonstrated
| Study | Method | Result | Significance |
|---|---|---|---|
| Nykänen et al. (2010) | Weights-of-Evidence + Logistic Regression, Yilgarn Ni | 81.6% of validation deposits in 9% of greenstone area | First large-scale Ni-specific MPM for Yilgarn |
| Maepa et al. (2024) | Deep Forest, gold, Sudan | AUC 0.964, <15 training samples | Proves feasibility with sparse labels |
| Liu et al. (2021) | Bagging-PU + Bayesian HPO | Outperforms RF on 3D mineral potential | Validates PU over standard classification |
| Li et al. (2024) | Enhanced GAN + PU bagging, lateritic Ni-Co, Eastern Australia | Improved AUC over standard PU | GAN augmentation helps with extreme label scarcity |
| Butterworth et al. (2025) | AI prospectivity, LCT pegmatites, WA | First regional-scale Li maps for WA; Li-Au-Ni proximity confirmed | Directly relevant to lithium target |
| CSIRO (2022) | ML on mineral chemistry, Ni sulfide indicators | Ni-depleted olivine + low-Ru chromite as key signatures | Geochemical feature engineering targets |
| Sun et al. (2023) | SHAP-based interpretable MPM framework | SHAP + PDP for geologist-facing output | Interpretability methodology |
| Zhang et al. (2025) | Geospatially dissimilar negative labels | Better spatial selectivity than distance-based | Current best practice for pseudo-negative selection |

### Model Performance Baseline (from literature)
- Random Forest: AUC ~0.91–0.93
- XGBoost: AUC ~0.91–0.94
- Logistic Regression: AUC ~0.82 (but 81.6% deposit capture in 9% area for Ni-specific)
- Deep Forest: AUC ~0.96 (but small sample)
- Bagging-PU consistently outperforms standard binary classification when deposit count is low (<200 positives)

