## Practical Implications

### ML Methodology: Positive-Unlabeled (PU) Learning
**Do not use standard binary classification.** Positive labels = confirmed OZMIN deposits. No reliable negatives exist (absence of known deposit ≠ absence of mineralisation). Treating unlabeled as negative introduces massive false-negative contamination.

**Bagging-PU** (Mordelet & Vert 2014): Train N classifiers, each on all positives + random unlabeled subset as pseudo-negatives. Average predictions. This hedges against label crossover.

**Negative selection (current best practice):** Select pseudo-negatives from geospatially dissimilar localities, not random pixels. Increases spatial selectivity.

### Model Stack
1. **XGBoost** (primary) — best empirical AUC, handles missing values, fast
2. **Random Forest** (baseline comparison)
3. **LightGBM** (large grid scaling)

### Interpretability Is Non-Negotiable
Geologists reject black boxes. Always compute SHAP values. Present: mean |SHAP| bar chart, partial dependence plots for top 5 features, spatial SHAP maps where feasible. Without this, the model has no path to industry adoption.

### Validation Must Be Spatial
Use `LeaveOneGroupOut` with geological terrane as group, or spatial block cross-validation. Never random split. Report both AUC-ROC and concentration-area (C-A) plots showing what % of area is needed to capture what % of deposits.

### Feature Engineering
| Feature | Source | Geological Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| TMI | Magnetic grid | Komatiite/mafic body mapping |
| FVD | TMI derivative | Shallow structure, contact mapping |
| Analytic signal | TMI derivative | Lithological boundaries regardless of remanence |
| Tilt angle | TMI derivative | Structural boundary mapping |
| Bouguer anomaly | Gravity grid | Bulk crustal density, mafic/ultramafic mass |
| Horizontal gradient magnitude | Gravity derivative | Fault zones, density contrasts |
| K | Radiometric | Potassic alteration around Ni systems |
| Th | Radiometric | Felsic crust (sulfur source proxy) |
| U | Radiometric | Complementary crustal proxy |
| K/Th ratio | Derived | Potassic alteration intensity — strong Ni indicator |
| Th/U ratio | Derived | Metamorphic grade proxy |
| F-parameter (K×Th/U) | Derived | Felsic contamination index — sulfur source |

